                designated home for a quantity DIGGS has already defined a dictionary entry for: it
                guarantees that parameterName carries a mandatory codeSpace
                (gml:CodeWithAuthorityType, inherited from diggs:AuthorizedParameterType), the
                discipline a closed enumeration gives a fixed vocabulary, applied to an open,
                dictionary-governed one. diggs:ParameterPropertyType remains correct for a genuine
                escape hatch, such as the other-property elements, where DIGGS has not defined the
                property. diggs:ProvenancedParameter is admitted alongside diggs:AuthorizedParameter
                because it extends it: it is an AuthorizedParameter that also states the subject and
                source of its value. See diggs:DesignRITreatedAreaType/methodApplicabilityRatio and
                diggs:ArchingCoefficientType/coefficient for worked cases.
